{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `log_radon`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the manual per-observation likelihood contribution `target += normal_lpdf(log_radon[n] | mu[n], sigma_y)` with a deterministic construction of `mu` followed by one vectorized built-in sampling statement, `log_radon ~ normal(mu, sigma_y)`. This preserves the same likelihood density. The predictors and indexing data (`floor_measure`, `county_idx`, `J`, and `N`) remain unprotected context inputs. No data changes were required.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> J;
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county_idx;
  vector[N] floor_measure;
  vector[N] log_radon;
}
parameters {
  real alpha;
  vector[J] beta;
  real mu_beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma_beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
}
model {
  vector[N] mu;
  // Prior
  alpha ~ normal(0, 10);
  sigma_y ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_beta ~ normal(0, 1);
  mu_beta ~ normal(0, 10);

  beta ~ normal(mu_beta, sigma_beta);
  for (n in 1 : N) {
    mu[n] = alpha + floor_measure[n] * beta[county_idx[n]];
  }
  log_radon ~ normal(mu, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":3,"N":1,"county_idx":[2],"floor_measure":[6.226191051538669],"log_radon":[4.476207763993235]}","protected_variables":["log_radon"]}
